## Phase 1 — Expand (additive)

*New column/table/index, always additive, with safe default values; a new constraint as
`NOT VALID` (or equivalent) if there is legacy data.*

| Change | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| {{e.g.-new-column-x}} | {{type-default-nullable}} |

**Down for this phase:** {{how-to-revert-the-expand-without-losing-data}}

## Phase 2 — Migrate data and code

*Backfill in batches if the volume demands it — never a single `UPDATE` that locks the table. Batch
failures are logged, not silent.*

| Step | Batch size | Progress check |
| --- | --- | --- |
| {{backfill-of-x}} | {{e.g.-50k-rows}} | {{how-to-measure-progress}} |

Backfill runbook: instantiate `templates/technical/runbook.md.template` at
`product/07-operations/runbooks/{{name}}.md`.

**Constraint validation** (if applicable): {{how-and-when-the-check-is-validated-after-backfill}}

